# `golem/interest`

**Spatial interest management:** a `Grid` (spatial hash with configurable cell size, Insert/Remove/Move/Query) and a `Manager` that tracks per-session fields of interest. `FOI` describes a circular area anchored to an entity with a radius and hysteresis margin. `Diff` holds per-session enter/stay/exit entity ID lists computed each tick plus `Space`, the session's space for that tick.

**`Manager`** owns the `Grid` and per-session known sets. Key methods: `AssignFOI(sessionID, entityID, radius, margin)` / `RemoveFOI(sessionID)` for lifecycle (`RemoveFOI` returns the cleared known set, now owned by the caller, so the Server can exit those entities on a later space transition); both maintain the `anchorFOIs` reverse index (anchor entity → sessions, empty entries dropped, reassignment moves the session), read by `AppendAnchoredSessions(dst, entityID)` so the Server finds the sessions a moved entity anchors without scanning every FOI; `UpdateGrid(registry)` synchronises the grid with all live entities (inserts new, removes stale, moves changed) and records deleted globals in reused `removedGlobals`; `ComputeDiffs()` returns a `map[sessionID]*Diff` by querying each session's FOI against the grid, applying hysteresis (enter at `Radius`, exit at `Radius+Margin`), and diffing against the previous known set. `ComputeDiffsFiltered(allow)` applies an optional predicate before Entered/Stayed and forces Exited when a previously known entity becomes disallowed; `ComputeDiffs()` remains equivalent to a nil (allow-all) filter. Global entities (`IsGlobal() == true`) bypass spatial checks but still pass through the allow predicate (Server supplies visibility-group membership). Deleted globals emit Exited via `removedGlobals` even when the FOI anchor is not on the grid. When the anchor is missing or global (globals-only branch, no spatial sweep), `exitStaleKnown` exits known entities that are no longer alive (`alive` from the last `UpdateGrid`, e.g. a deleted former anchor) on both the single-space and spaced paths; live local entities of the session's space stay known (frozen). The normal grid-anchor path is unchanged. This package does not store group policy.

**Spaces:** the Manager keeps one grid per space (`grid` is space 0; other grids are created on demand and dropped when empty), space-0 `globals` plus `globalsBySpace`, `entitySpace` (non-zero spaces of tracked entities and globals) and `sessionSpace` (non-zero last space of FOI sessions). `UpdateGrid` runs the single-space loop over `Registry.All()` while `!SpacesInUse()` and no entity was left outside space 0 (rechecking after the read); otherwise it reads `AppendSpaced` once into the reused `spacedBuf` (cleared at the end of `updateGridSpaced`, so it keeps capacity but no entity pointers) and moves entities between grids and global sets. `ComputeDiffsFiltered` resolves each session's space from its anchor (on a grid or global), else keeps the last space (`SetSessionSpace` seeds it; `SessionSpace` and `SessionFOI` read it), then queries only that space's grid and globals. Known entities outside the space exit: non-candidates and other-space globals through the known sweep, and live other-space entities explicitly in the missing-anchor globals-only branch (`exitStaleKnown`). After every call each known set lies inside its `Diff.Space`. With no spaced entities and no non-zero session space both methods skip all space lookups.

**Not thread-safe.** All methods are called exclusively from the game tick goroutine (single-writer), under Server `interestMu`. The parent **`golem`** package creates and drives the Manager inside `runLoop`; consumers interact via `Server.AssignFOI` / `Server.RemoveFOI`.

**Grid membership:** private addToCell/removeFromCell helpers own cell-map creation, membership changes, and empty-cell pruning. Insert/Move/Remove own the position and cellOf indexes. Same-cell Move updates the position without rehashing. UpdateGrid uses Insert's existing insert-or-move contract; global policy and stale-entity cleanup remain in Manager.

Depends on **`golem/registry`** for the `Entity` interface, `SpaceID`, `Registry.All()`, `SpacesInUse()` and `AppendSpaced()`. Does **not** import `golem`, `golem/net`, `golem/visibility`, or `golem/world`.
